<Section id="story" title="It started with a blurry photo" intro="In 2019, a hiker left a bag of homemade oat clusters on a stump near the Cedar trailhead. The next morning it was gone, and there was one very large footprint.">
	<div class="prose">
		<p>That hiker was our founder, Juniper Hale. The oat clusters became Pine Cone Crunch, and the footprint became our logo. We now make six snacks in a converted ranger station in Bend, Oregon, and mail them to hikers in all fifty states.</p>
		<p>We cook in small batches, we buy oats and berries from farms in the Pacific Northwest, and we test every recipe on the trail before it ships.</p>
	</div>
</Section>

<Section id="witness" title="Why we keep doing it" tone="raised">
	<Testimonial name="Juniper Hale" where="founder">I still leave a bag on that stump every spring. It's always gone by morning.</Testimonial>
</Section>
